WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.039
Apollo Q Labs. Level three, module two: theta, vega, rho and I V crush.

2
00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:14.679
Theta is time decay, the loss of value as time passes: the change in option price from one calendar day passing.

3
00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:20.973
Long options, ones you bought, usually have negative theta, and short options, ones you sold, positive.

4
00:00:20.973 --> 00:00:32.793
Decay is not linear, meaning not steady: it speeds up in the last weeks, especially for at the money options, with a strike, the price the option lets you buy or sell at, near the stock price.

5
00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:44.977
Example: an option at three fifty with theta of minus point oh three. Tomorrow it is about three forty seven, all else equal: minus three dollars per contract per day.

6
00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:51.935
Every day costs option buyers money if the stock stands still, and the cost accelerates in the last thirty days.

7
00:00:51.935 --> 00:00:57.909
Use the days slider, the control for days remaining, to see how much time decay costs your trade.

8
00:00:58.209 --> 00:01:08.771
Vega is about volatility: the change in option price for a one point change in implied volatility, the expected yearly move priced into options.

9
00:01:08.771 --> 00:01:18.500
Long options gain when I V rises. Short options gain when I V falls. Longer dated options, with more time left, have more vega.

10
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:27.953
Example: vega point one two. After earnings, a company’s results report, I V drops from sixty to forty percent, minus twenty points.

11
00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:40.861
The option loses about two forty, or two hundred and forty dollars per contract, even if the stock did not move. This is I V crush, a sharp drop in I V after an event, which lowers option prices.

12
00:01:41.161 --> 00:01:49.077
I V often drops sharply right after earnings or other known events. That lowers every option’s price at once.

13
00:01:49.077 --> 00:01:57.484
Long options can lose money even when the stock moves your way. Check vega in the Greeks table, the app’s list of these measures.

14
00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:03.289
Rho is about interest rates: the change in option price for a one point change in rates.

15
00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:22.043
Calls, the right to buy 100 shares at the strike, gain and puts, the right to sell 100 shares at the strike, lose when rates rise. Rho matters mostly for long dated options, called LEAPS (options that expire a year or more away), and is usually the smallest Greek, the smallest of these measures.

16
00:02:22.343 --> 00:02:34.739
Recap: theta is daily time decay, faster near the end. Vega is sensitivity to I V, and I V crush can hit after events. Rho is interest rates, usually the smallest.

17
00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:38.601
Next, read the lessons, then take the six question quiz.

